{% comment %}
  Spares Plus (CLI-694): honeypot spam trap for the enquiry forms.

  Usage: {% render 'form-honeypot' %} immediately inside a {% form 'contact' %}.

  A field no human can see or tab to. Bots that fill every input give themselves
  away, and global.js cancels the submit when it has a value.

  Deliberately NOT `display: none` / `hidden` / `type="hidden"`: the better spam
  bots skip anything hidden that way, and a hidden input is not what they look
  for. It is positioned off-screen instead, with aria-hidden and tabindex="-1"
  so assistive technology and keyboard users never reach it.

  This is a deterrent, not a guarantee. Shopify's contact form has no
  server-side hook, so the check can only run in the browser - a bot posting
  straight to /contact#ContactForm bypasses it entirely. Real protection would
  need a CAPTCHA (Shopify's own, under Settings > Customer privacy) or an app.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="form-honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
  <label for="ContactFormWebsite-{{ honeypot_id | default: 'default' }}">
    Leave this field empty
  </label>
  <input
    type="text"
    id="ContactFormWebsite-{{ honeypot_id | default: 'default' }}"
    name="contact[Leave this field empty]"
    value=""
    tabindex="-1"
    autocomplete="off"
  >
</div>
